{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"decagonal-indisposed-tamarin","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nTwo accepted reliability oracles still consume multi-second wall time per matrix cell: test_slow_but_progressing_remote_is_not_aborted deliberately serves for 15 seconds (15.1s in current macOS CI; original behavior ticket suave-constant-cow), and test_read_retried_then_terminal uses one-second timeout/grace/drain windows across retries (9.06s; original behavior ticket fizzy-trunk-salt). Their real process/socket coverage is load-bearing, but the production-scale durations are not.\n\n## Plan\nRetain one real socket/process-group sentinel for each mechanism while injecting smaller test-only stall, timeout, grace, and drain windows with generous scheduling headroom. Keep semantic attempt/reap/throughput assertions and use polling rather than brittle absolute-time pass conditions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Slow-progress still crosses a full configured low-speed window and proves throughput, not elapsed wall time, prevents abort.\n- [ ] ACLI read still spawns exactly the production retry count and proves every process group is reaped.\n- [ ] Production timeout/stall defaults are unchanged.\n- [ ] The focused tests retain real subprocess/socket execution but complete in low single-digit seconds on macOS CI.\n- [ ] No absolute upper-bound assertion is tightened into a loaded-runner flake.","id":"baeb-4f4b-3227-457e","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["ci","performance","tests","reliability"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Shrink test-only real-time windows in subprocess and network sentinels"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786598942661292001,"uuid":"f0d64690-ed16-42d3-bb8e-1ed17a1f2d0e"}